# Assignment 3: Student Management Portal

An end-to-end, console-based **Student Management Portal** written in core Python (no external libraries). It lets an administrator log in and manage student records through an interactive menu. All data is stored in plain text files, so records are kept between runs.

**Course:** Programming for AI (PAI)
**Author:** [Your Name] ([25L-XXXX])

---

## Features

- Login with a limit of 3 attempts
- Add a student (ID, name, course, marks)
- Search students by ID or part of a name
- Update a student's marks
- Delete a student
- View all students in a table
- Generate a report (total, average, highest, lowest, grade distribution) and save it to `report.txt`
- **Own feature:** rank students from highest to lowest marks (bubble sort)

## Python concepts demonstrated

| Concept | Where it is used |
|---|---|
| Functions (`def`) with parameters and `return` | `user_login()`, `add_record()`, `search_record()`, `generate_report()`, and others |
| Loops (`while`, `for`) | `while True` main menu loop; `for` loops for loading, searching, reporting and ranking |
| File handling (read, write, append) | `load_students()`, `save_students()`, `append_student()`, `save_report()` |
| Exception handling (`try`, `except`, `finally`) | `FileNotFoundError`, `PermissionError`, `ValueError` handled so the program never crashes |

